    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/2/92415.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 4,
    "turn_text": "Yeah, I think what we have to do, I'm an armed services committee in the Senate. What I always say to everybody is step one is what's our purpose? What threats are we facing right now? And do we have the right, you know, the trained men and women? And do we have the right equipment for them for today's issues? And so that's why I try to push every year as we go through the defense budget, knowing that Florida is a great place, whether it's for our Navy or for our Air Force to be stationed because people want to be in our state. When I was governor, I focused on making sure we were the state that everybody wanted to be stationed and everybody wanted to retire. So we have 22 military bases in our state and three defined commands. And our 20 military bases and three to five commands and I made sure that we folks on every one of those how our communities could be a better partner with our bases and our bases could be a partner with our communities.",
